Package: mitmproxy
Version: mitmproxy_VERSION-BUILD_VERSION~DIST
Architecture: SUPPORTED_ARCHITECTURES
Description: interactive TLS-capable intercepting HTTP proxy
 mitmproxy is a free and open source interactive HTTPS proxy for penetration
 testers and software developers. It intercepts, inspects, modifies and
 replays HTTP/1, HTTP/2, HTTP/3, WebSocket and raw TCP/UDP traffic, generating
 TLS interception certificates on the fly.
 .
 This package installs three commands:
  - mitmproxy: interactive console interface for inspecting and editing
    traffic flows on the fly
  - mitmdump: command-line version, "tcpdump for HTTP"
  - mitmweb: web-based interface served on http://127.0.0.1:8081
 .
 Regular, transparent, reverse, upstream, SOCKS5, WireGuard and local capture
 modes are supported, and traffic can be scripted with Python addons.
 .
 These are upstream's self-contained standalone builds, which bundle their own
 Python interpreter and OpenSSL, so no Python packages are required. Addon
 scripts can only import modules shipped inside the bundle.
